---
/**
 * Transformer block lesson — illustration #1.
 *
 * The modern Pre-LN block layout: LayerNorm before each sub-layer
 * (rather than after, which was the original 2017 Post-LN pattern).
 * Pre-LN is the de-facto standard since GPT-2 because it trains stably
 * at depth without elaborate warmup. Attention and FFN sub-layers each
 * sit between LayerNorm-on-input and an additive residual back to the
 * sub-layer's pre-norm input. Position encoding is added before any
 * block (shown as a separate input row); the block itself doesn't add
 * it.
 */
---

<figure class="cw-illus">
	<svg viewBox="0 0 800 460" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" role="img" aria-labelledby="tb-title tb-desc">
		<title id="tb-title">A complete transformer block</title>
		<desc id="tb-desc">A vertical block diagram. At the top, the input enters the block at dimension d_model (this is the embedding plus position encoding). The input flows through multi-head attention, then through an "Add and Norm" step that adds the input back as a residual connection and applies layer normalization. The result flows through a feed-forward network, then through another "Add and Norm" with another residual. The output exits at dimension d_model, ready to feed the next block. Two residual arcs show how the input bypasses each sublayer.</desc>

		<defs>
			<marker id="cw-arrow-tb" viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="9" refY="5" markerWidth="8" markerHeight="8" orient="auto">
				<path d="M 0 0 L 10 5 L 0 10 z" fill="currentColor"/>
			</marker>
			<marker id="cw-arrow-tb-accent" viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="9" refY="5" markerWidth="8" markerHeight="8" orient="auto">
				<path d="M 0 0 L 10 5 L 0 10 z" fill="#7c3aed"/>
			</marker>
		</defs>

		<rect x="290" y="20" width="220" height="40" rx="6" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5"/>
		<text x="400" y="38" text-anchor="middle" font-family="ui-sans-serif, system-ui, sans-serif" font-size="13" fill="currentColor">input (d_model)</text>
		<text x="400" y="52" text-anchor="middle" font-family="ui-sans-serif, system-ui, sans-serif" font-size="10" fill="currentColor" opacity="0.6" font-style="italic">embedding + position encoding</text>

		<line x1="400" y1="60" x2="400" y2="86" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" marker-end="url(#cw-arrow-tb)"/>

		<rect x="290" y="90" width="220" height="44" rx="6" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5"/>
		<text x="400" y="110" text-anchor="middle" font-family="ui-sans-serif, system-ui, sans-serif" font-size="13" fill="currentColor">Multi-Head Attention</text>
		<text x="400" y="125" text-anchor="middle" font-family="ui-sans-serif, system-ui, sans-serif" font-size="10" fill="currentColor" opacity="0.6" font-style="italic">cross-token mixing</text>

		<path d="M 290 40 L 220 40 L 220 156 L 290 156" fill="none" stroke="#7c3aed" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-dasharray="4 3" marker-end="url(#cw-arrow-tb-accent)"/>
		<text x="180" y="100" text-anchor="end" font-family="ui-sans-serif, system-ui, sans-serif" font-size="11" font-style="italic" fill="#7c3aed">residual</text>

		<line x1="400" y1="134" x2="400" y2="148" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" marker-end="url(#cw-arrow-tb)"/>

		<rect x="290" y="148" width="220" height="36" rx="6" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5"/>
		<text x="400" y="170" text-anchor="middle" font-family="ui-sans-serif, system-ui, sans-serif" font-size="13" fill="currentColor">Add + LayerNorm</text>

		<line x1="400" y1="184" x2="400" y2="210" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" marker-end="url(#cw-arrow-tb)"/>

		<rect x="290" y="214" width="220" height="44" rx="6" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5"/>
		<text x="400" y="234" text-anchor="middle" font-family="ui-sans-serif, system-ui, sans-serif" font-size="13" fill="currentColor">Feed-Forward Network</text>
		<text x="400" y="249" text-anchor="middle" font-family="ui-sans-serif, system-ui, sans-serif" font-size="10" fill="currentColor" opacity="0.6" font-style="italic">per-token MLP, adds nonlinearity</text>

		<path d="M 290 166 L 220 166 L 220 280 L 290 280" fill="none" stroke="#7c3aed" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-dasharray="4 3" marker-end="url(#cw-arrow-tb-accent)"/>
		<text x="180" y="226" text-anchor="end" font-family="ui-sans-serif, system-ui, sans-serif" font-size="11" font-style="italic" fill="#7c3aed">residual</text>

		<line x1="400" y1="258" x2="400" y2="272" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" marker-end="url(#cw-arrow-tb)"/>

		<rect x="290" y="272" width="220" height="36" rx="6" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5"/>
		<text x="400" y="294" text-anchor="middle" font-family="ui-sans-serif, system-ui, sans-serif" font-size="13" fill="currentColor">Add + LayerNorm</text>

		<line x1="400" y1="308" x2="400" y2="334" stroke="#7c3aed" stroke-width="2" marker-end="url(#cw-arrow-tb-accent)"/>

		<rect x="290" y="338" width="220" height="40" rx="6" fill="none" stroke="#7c3aed" stroke-width="2"/>
		<text x="400" y="356" text-anchor="middle" font-family="ui-sans-serif, system-ui, sans-serif" font-size="13" fill="#7c3aed" font-weight="600">block output (d_model)</text>
		<text x="400" y="370" text-anchor="middle" font-family="ui-sans-serif, system-ui, sans-serif" font-size="10" fill="#7c3aed" opacity="0.85" font-style="italic">feeds next block (or final output)</text>

		<text x="400" y="410" text-anchor="middle" font-family="ui-sans-serif, system-ui, sans-serif" font-size="11" fill="currentColor" opacity="0.6" font-style="italic">a single block; a transformer stacks N copies</text>
		<text x="400" y="430" text-anchor="middle" font-family="ui-sans-serif, system-ui, sans-serif" font-size="10" fill="currentColor" opacity="0.5" font-style="italic">(modern variants often use Pre-LN: LayerNorm before each sublayer instead of after)</text>
	</svg>
	<figcaption>One transformer block. Multi-head attention does the cross-token mixing; the feed-forward network adds non-linearity per token; the two residual connections let gradients and information flow around each sub-layer; layer normalization keeps the activations well-behaved. A real transformer stacks many of these.</figcaption>
</figure>

<style>
	.cw-illus { margin: 1.75rem auto; max-width: 100%; }
	.cw-illus svg { display: block; width: 100%; max-width: 780px; height: auto; margin: 0 auto; }
	.cw-illus figcaption { text-align: center; font-size: 0.85rem; opacity: 0.75; margin-top: 0.5rem; font-style: italic; }
</style>
